00:05:46,666 --> 00:05:52,666
Courage is immortal.

2
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:39,333
Mortal is a action, fantasy, thriller film directed by André Øvredal.

3
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
A young boy must discover the origins of his extraordinary powers before he is captured
by authorities hell-bent on condemning him for an accidental murder.

4
00:23:06,666 --> 00:23:12,666
Eric, played by Nat Wolff.

5
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:59,333
Christine, played by Iben Akerlie.

6
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Henrik, played by Per Frisch.

7
00:40:26,666 --> 00:40:32,666
Hathaway, played by Priyanka Bose.

8
00:46:13,333 --> 00:46:19,333
Ole, played by Arthur Hakalahti.

9
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
PST Officer, played by Kai Kolstad Rødseth.

10
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
Mortal (Norwegian: Torden) is a 2020 fantasy action film
co-written and directed by André Øvredal.

11
01:03:33,333 --> 01:03:39,333
The film is inspired by Norse mythology, and stars Nat Wolff.

12
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
It is supported by a grant from the Government of Norway.

13
01:15:06,666 --> 01:15:12,666
The film's dialogue is in English and Norwegian, and most of the actors are
Norwegian with the exception of Wolff and Priyanka Bose.

14
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
The film's original music by Marcus Paus was nominated for the Amanda Award and was
the Norwegian nominee for the Nordic Film Music Days – HARPA Award.

15
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
Mortal was released in Norway on 28 February 2020, by Nordisk Films, in the United Kingdom on 20
August, by Signature Entertainment, and in the United States on 10 November, by Saban Films.

16
01:32:26,666 --> 01:32:32,666
It received mixed reviews from critics.

17
01:38:13,333 --> 01:38:19,333
The tone is intense.
